1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
Let's say you have an accident and hurt

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:02,860
your leg.

3
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,340
You think it might be broken,

4
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:06,460
so someone calls an ambulance.

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,900
If it's not life-threatening,

6
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,620
the paramedics may ask:

7
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,540
public or private hospital?

8
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,660
Without private insurance, going private means paying the

9
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:18,060
whole bill yourself, often thousands of dollars.

10
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,140
So you say:

11
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:19,900
public.

12
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,100
At the public hospital,

13
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,660
they confirm it's broken.

14
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,220
You have surgery to set it,

15
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,447
they put on a plaster,

16
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:26,593
and you're sent home.

17
00:00:26,613 --> 00:00:29,180
"See your GP in four weeks." Four weeks

18
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,900
later, your GP cuts off the plaster.

19
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,180
It still hurts.

20
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,860
So you get an X-ray.

21
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,220
Back at the GP:

22
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,767
"It hasn't healed properly.

23
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:39,900
You need to see an orthopaedic specialist,

24
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,100
a bone doctor.

25
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,020
Do you have private health insurance?" "No." "Then

26
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,700
the wait to see the specialist will be

27
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,007
longer." You go on the waiting list,

28
00:00:48,027 --> 00:00:50,833
and you wait… and wait.

29
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:52,580
Finally, the specialist says:

30
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,380
"This needs another operation.

31
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,300
Do you have private insurance?

32
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:56,807
No?

33
00:00:56,827 --> 00:00:59,153
Then the public waiting list could be months.

34
00:00:59,173 --> 00:01:00,487
And if you wait that long,

35
00:01:00,507 --> 00:01:02,380
the bone may heal the wrong way for

36
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,180
good." And it's not an emergency anymore,

37
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,860
so you can't just go back to the

38
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,113
emergency department.

39
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:10,140
You're back on a waiting list.

40
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:11,740
Your other option is to pay for it

41
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:13,260
privately yourself.

42
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,833
The surgeon says it will cost,

43
00:01:14,853 --> 00:01:17,580
for example, seven thousand dollars.

44
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,327
So:

45
00:01:18,347 --> 00:01:20,700
wait, and risk it healing wrong forever,

46
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:21,980
or pay?

47
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,700
Now picture someone with private hospital cover.

48
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:27,473
Same accident, same visit to the specialist.

49
00:01:27,493 --> 00:01:30,300
"Do you have private insurance?" "Yes." "Great,

50
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,940
we can operate next week." Their fund helps

51
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:33,980
pay the bill.

52
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,820
They may still pay an excess or a

53
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,553
gap, but they're fixed,

54
00:01:37,573 --> 00:01:39,500
healed, and back on their feet.

55
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:41,500
This might not matter for everyone.

56
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:43,287
But if you rely on your job,

57
00:01:43,307 --> 00:01:45,340
can you afford months off waiting?

58
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:46,727
Or would you need a loan,

59
00:01:46,747 --> 00:01:48,780
just to get fixed so you can work?

60
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:51,420
That's the real point of private health insurance:

61
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,620
a safety net.

62
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:55,020
The party fund is already there when something

63
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,007
goes wrong.

64
00:01:56,027 --> 00:01:56,780
But wait:

65
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:00,087
some private hospitals do have emergency departments.

66
00:02:00,107 --> 00:02:01,660
What happens if you go to one with

67
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,540
insurance?

68
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,753
I heard you still have to pay anyway!

69
00:02:04,773 --> 00:02:06,060
So what's the point?

70
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,500
Find out in our next video!
